## 8\. Simulation Findings & Constants

### 8.1 Board Sizing
| R | Cells | Ship density | First-hit (turns, salvo=2) | Verdict |
|----|----|----|----|----|
| 5 | 91 | 18.7% | \~3 | Too cramped |
| 6 | 127 | 13.4% | \~4 | Borderline |
| **7** | **169** | **10.1%** | **\~5** | ✅ **Recommended** |
| **8** | **217** | **7.8%** | **\~6** | ✅ Alternate |
| 9 | 271 | 6.3% | \~7 | Borderline sparse |
| 10 | 331 | 5.1% | \~10 | Too sparse |


### 8.2 Cycle Lengths Under Wrap (R=8)
| Heading | Cycle length | % of board covered |
|----|----|----|
| S (0, +1) | **217** (Hamiltonian) | 100% |
| SE (+1, 0) | 26 | 12% |
| NE (+1, -1) | 25–42 (varies by start) | 12–19% |


**Design implication:** Heading choice is a meaningful defender strategy axis. Long-cycle headings give better board coverage but more predictable returns. Short-cycle headings are stealthier but revisit sooner.

### 8.3 Collision Frequency

With 5-ship fleet, random headings, R=8, cd=2:

* **31% of turns** have ≥1 collision (multi-ship cell overlap)
* Only **1% of games** have zero collisions across 80 turns
* With size-based cooldowns: rises to **34%**

### 8.4 Same-Cell Revisit Timing

For a size-4, cooldown-2 ship on a 26-step cycle at R=8:

* Occupancy window per cell: **8 consecutive turns** (`size × cooldown`)
* Gap between revisits: **44 turns** (`(cycle_len − size) × cooldown`)
* 17 of 26 trajectory cells get multi-visited in 80 turns


