## 12\. Prior Art

The moving-shapes-with-hidden-course direction is **essentially untrodden** in published Battleship variants:
| Mechanic | Found in any published variant? |
|----|----|
| Hex grid | ✅ (2008 Hasbro — but static ships, split board) |
| Moving ships with hidden course | ❌ (only "announced move" or "free teleport") |
| Damage slows movement | ❌ |
| Persistent "footprint" trail as inference signal | ❌ |
| Torus wrap boundary | ❌ |
| Salvo with spread patterns | ❌ (Salvo variant exists but fires 3 free probes) |


The closest cousin is a variant where ships move in orthogonal directions but **the move must be announced** — the designers seemingly chose announcement because they didn't solve the imperfect-information bookkeeping. The **footprint mechanic** (timestamped hit marks as breadcrumb trail) is exactly the missing piece that lets movement stay hidden while giving the attacker inferential traction.



